<title>USA: Biopharmaceutics enters $7.5 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Biopharmaceutics enters $7.5 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>BELLPORT, N.Y. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Biopharmaceutics Inc said on Thursday that it had entered into a letter of intent to acquire privately owned Caribbean Medical Testing Center in Puerto Rico for $7.5 million.</p>
<p>Biopharmaceutics said the transaction, to take the form of cash and notes, is subject to the availability of adequate financing and is expected to be signed by June 12.</p>
<p>CMT is a specialty medical testing center and reference laboratory. Biopharmaceutics Inc specializes in contract pharmaceutical manufacturing and marketing of feminine hygiene and family planning products.</p>
</text>
